Lab 3: Monitoring & Alerting with Prometheus, Grafana, and AI
Objective
Set up Prometheus and Grafana to monitor system metrics, collect time-series data, and apply AI models to forecast future resource usage or detect early warning signs of system issues.

Prerequisites
Start your Al Nafi-provided Ubuntu machine
Install Prometheus:
sudo useradd --no-create-home --shell /bin/false prometheus
sudo mkdir /etc/prometheus /var/lib/prometheus

cd /tmp
wget https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/releases/download/v2.52.0/prometheus-2.52.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar xvf prometheus-2.52.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
cd prometheus-2.52.0.linux-amd64

sudo cp prometheus /usr/local/bin/
sudo cp promtool /usr/local/bin/
sudo cp -r consoles/ console_libraries/ /etc/prometheus/
sudo cp prometheus.yml /etc/prometheus/
Create a systemd service (optional) or run manually:

prometheus --config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Access Prometheus at: http://localhost:9090

Install Node Exporter (for system metrics):
cd /tmp
wget https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/releases/download/v1.7.0/node_exporter-1.7.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar xvf node_exporter-1.7.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
cd node_exporter-1.7.0.linux-amd64
./node_exporter
Prometheus config (/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml) should include:

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'node'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['localhost:9100']
Install Grafana:
sudo apt install -y software-properties-common
sudo add-apt-repository "deb https://packages.grafana.com/oss/deb stable main"
wget -q -O - https://packages.grafana.com/gpg.key | sudo apt-key add -
sudo apt update
sudo apt install grafana -y
sudo systemctl start grafana-server
sudo systemctl enable grafana-server
Access Grafana at: http://localhost:3000
Login: admin / admin

Steps
Step 1: Monitor System Metrics
In Grafana, add Prometheus as a data source (http://localhost:9090).

Create a dashboard and plot:

CPU usage (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode!="idle"}[1m]))

Memory usage (node_memory_Active_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes)

Step 2: Collect Metrics for AI Analysis
Prometheus query API:

curl 'http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query_range?query=node_memory_MemFree_bytes&start=<START>&end=<END>&step=15'
Save data to CSV via Python:

import requests
import pandas as pd
import time

end = int(time.time())
start = end - 3600  # last 1 hour

url = f"http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query_range?query=node_memory_MemFree_bytes&start={start}&end={end}&step=15"
resp = requests.get(url).json()

values = resp['data']['result'][0]['values']
df = pd.DataFrame(values, columns=["timestamp", "mem_free"])
df["timestamp"] = pd.to_datetime(df["timestamp"], unit='s')
df["mem_free"] = df["mem_free"].astype(float)
df.to_csv("mem_free_data.csv", index=False)
Step 3: Predict Future Usage Using AI
Install ML tools:

pip install pandas scikit-learn matplotlib
Create prediction script:

import pandas as pd
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import numpy as np

df = pd.read_csv("mem_free_data.csv")
df["time_idx"] = range(len(df))

X = df[["time_idx"]]
y = df["mem_free"]

model = LinearRegression()
model.fit(X, y)

future = pd.DataFrame({"time_idx": range(len(df), len(df)+20)})
future["mem_free_pred"] = model.predict(future)

plt.plot(df["time_idx"], y, label="Actual")
plt.plot(future["time_idx"], future["mem_free_pred"], label="Predicted", linestyle="--")
plt.xlabel("Time Index")
plt.ylabel("Memory Free (bytes)")
plt.title("Memory Forecast")
plt.legend()
plt.savefig("memory_forecast.png")
plt.show()
